cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use RangerDanger in academic work, training material, or
  research, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "RangerDanger: an OT/ICS cyber range for hands-on substation network segmentation training"
abstract: >-
  RangerDanger is a containerized cyber range that simulates an
  electric distribution substation — multi-zone networks, field
  devices speaking Modbus and DNP3, a multi-homed supervisory
  controller, and a real DPI-capable firewall (containd) at the
  edge. Students work through seven guided labs covering
  baseline traffic analysis, segmentation requirements, remediation
  planning under a labor budget, hands-on firewall implementation,
  validation of the hardened reference, and post-change validation
  with PCAP evidence collection. The optional 2.3-bonus lab demonstrates
  an enterprise-to-vendor-to-field pivot using RDP/VNC, showing both
  the perimeter rule and defense-in-depth.
